# 0161: the harvester's ore search is gamemd's FootClass::Scan_For_Tiberium (FUN_004DD0A0).
#
# Read from the reverse-engineered description in github.com/YuriPlanet/vera20k
# (src/sim/miner/ore_scan.rs, read only): the miner's own cell when it holds tiberium; else rings
# r = 1..range-1 around it (the bound itself is not scanned), each walked i = -r..r over (x+i,y-r),
# (x+i,y+r), (x-r,y+i), (x+r,y+i). A cell with a strictly higher Get_Tiberium_Value (FUN_00485020:
# the type's Value= times overlay data + 1) replaces the best, and the first ring with a hit ends
# the scan. Ours took the first cell in raster order of the nearest Chebyshev ring and ignored what
# was in it, so a gem cell or a thick patch next to a thin one lost to whichever came first.
# find_reachable_ore keeps the zone flood, the occupant filter and the skip cell, and takes the
# Value= pair (OreValues) from step_harvest. Slave miners use the default pair.
# Real-data economy probe (PROBE_ECON, xmp31s2): unchanged within noise (1 HARV 4500 credits in 240 s,
# 3 HARV 7500).

